Adds a front-coded representation for pool-bundle value strings (pool .res
formatVersion 4), written by oven-sh/WebKit's icu/compress-data.ts +
icu/frontcode.ts. A formatVersion-3 pool bundle's 16-bit area is the tree's
shared string blob, read on the locale lookup path of every member bundle;
55% of it is prefixes shared with the lexicographic neighbor, redundancy
that ships raw today (the pools are keep-raw: compressing them would cost a
per-process decode).

Format and invariants: see the header of icu/frontcode.ts. The reader adds
one branch to the two functions that resolve pool string offsets
(res_getStringNoTrace, isNoInheritanceMarker): offsets below the pool's
verbatim limit (the traced startup / first-Intl hot set plus anything a
member must address with a small poolStringIndex16Limit) take exactly
today's path; higher offsets are ids into the front-coded region, decoded
one 16-string block at a time, on first access, into a side arena provided
by Bun's data archive (weak symbols, with their exact sizes; a package that
claims a slice the archive did not allocate is rejected). Without the
archive (ICU tools) the tables are uprv_malloc'ed once per pool.
Materialized strings use the stock string-v2 encoding and, like the
strings they replace, live for the whole process (consumers hold read-only
aliases into resource strings well past ures_flushCache). Every
header-derived offset and length is validated against the region the
pool's own indexes declare before it is used; a stock ICU rejects a
formatVersion-4 pool with U_INVALID_FORMAT_ERROR.

bun_icu_fc_materialized_blocks counts block decodes; icu/test-package.cpp
fails the image build if the startup / first-Intl phase materializes any
block (i.e. icu/pin-strings.txt no longer covers that path).

Scope: formatVersion-4 pools exist only inside Bun's repacked common-data
package, whose compact TOC (icu/ucmndata-toc.patch) ICU's package tools
cannot open. ures_swap and toolutil's pkgitems therefore never see one
(ures_swap rejects formatVersion 4 loudly; the package is little-endian
only, like everything else this pipeline emits). The packer always keeps
the "no inheritance" marker string verbatim, so isNoInheritanceMarker only
ever sees genrb's own encoding of it.
